<h2 class="mb-3"><i class="bi bi-diagram-3 me-2 text-primary"></i>Architecture</h2>

<p>
    The solution follows a <strong>Clean / Onion architecture</strong>. Dependencies point inward:
    the UI knows about Application and Infrastructure, Infrastructure implements the interfaces
    that Domain and Application declare, and Domain knows nothing about anyone else.
</p>

<div class="row g-4 mb-4">
    <div class="col-lg-8">
        <table class="table table-hover">
            <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">Project</th>
                <th scope="col">Responsibility</th>
            </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>ProjectZero</code> (web)</td>
                <td>Blazor UI, routing, layout, static assets. Depends on Application, Infrastructure and Shared.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>Core.Application</code></td>
                <td>Use cases: commands, queries, handlers, DTOs, the <code>IMediator</code> abstraction and MediatR registration.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>Core.Infrastructure</code></td>
                <td>Persistence: EF Core <code>DbContext</code>, repositories, unit of work and domain service implementations.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>Core.Domain</code></td>
                <td>The heart of the system: entities, aggregates, value objects, domain events and repository interfaces.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>Shared</code></td>
                <td>Contracts and types shared across layers.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>Tests/*</code></td>
                <td>Five test projects mirroring every layer — unit tests with xUnit, component tests with bUnit.</td>
            </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <div class="col-lg-4">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-header">Dependency direction</div>
            <div class="card-body">
<pre><code>ProjectZero  (UI)
    |
    v
Core.Infrastructure   Core.Application
    |       \         /      |
    v        v       v       v
      Core.Domain  &lt;-  Shared</code></pre>
                <p class="text-muted small mb-0">
                    Everything flows toward <code>Core.Domain</code> — the dependency rule of Clean Architecture.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<hr/>

<h2 class="mb-3"><i class="bi bi-puzzle me-2 text-primary"></i>Design patterns in use</h2>

<div class="row row-cols-1 row-cols-md-2 row-cols-lg-3 g-4 mb-4">
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="card-title fs-6"><i class="bi bi-box-seam me-2 text-primary"></i>Domain-Driven Design</h3>
                <p class="card-text text-muted small">
                    <code>Product</code> is an <code>AggregateRoot</code> with a private constructor and a factory
                    (<code>Product.Create</code>). State changes raise domain events.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="card-title fs-6"><i class="bi bi-arrow-left-right me-2 text-primary"></i>CQRS</h3>
                <p class="card-text text-muted small">
                    Commands (<code>CreateProductCommand</code>) and queries (<code>GetProductsQuery</code>) are separated into
                    <code>Features/Products/...</code> folders, each with its own handler.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="card-title fs-6"><i class="bi bi-cpu me-2 text-primary"></i>Mediator</h3>
                <p class="card-text text-muted small">
                    A custom <code>IMediator</code> (<code>SendAsync</code>/<code>QueryAsync</code>) provides the
                    entry point, and MediatR 14.2.0 wires the handlers.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="card-title fs-6"><i class="bi bi-database me-2 text-primary"></i>Repository</h3>
                <p class="card-text text-muted small">
                    <code>IProductRepository</code> lives in Domain, <code>ProductRepository</code> lives in Infrastructure.
                    Domain is never coupled to EF Core.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="card-title fs-6"><i class="bi bi-stack me-2 text-primary"></i>Unit of Work</h3>
                <p class="card-text text-muted small">
                    <code>IUnitOfWork.SaveChangesAsync</code> commits the transaction and flushes domain events in one place.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="card-title fs-6"><i class="bi bi-plug me-2 text-primary"></i>Dependency injection</h3>
                <p class="card-text text-muted small">
                    <code>AddApplicationServices()</code> and <code>AddInfrastructureServices()</code> extension methods
                    centralize every registration.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="card-title fs-6"><i class="bi bi-folder2-open me-2 text-primary"></i>Feature folders</h3>
                <p class="card-text text-muted small">
                    Each use case owns its command/query, handler and (optionally) DTO — cohesive and easy to delete.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="card-title fs-6"><i class="bi bi-arrow-repeat me-2 text-primary"></i>Factory method</h3>
                <p class="card-text text-muted small">
                    <code>Product.Create(name, fileName, price, description)</code> encapsulates validation and construction instead of a public constructor.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
        <div class="card h-100">
            <div class="card-body">
                <h3 class="card-title fs-6"><i class="bi bi-shuffle me-2 text-primary"></i>DTO mapping</h3>
                <p class="card-text text-muted small">
                    <code>GetProductsQueryHandler</code> maps the <code>Product</code> entity to a <code>ProductDto</code>,
                    keeping domain models private to the core.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

